# ~/.rgignore — extra ignore rules for ripgrep.
#
# ripgrep reads this file from any parent directory, with HIGHER precedence than
# a repo's .gitignore. Because it's stowed to $HOME, it applies to every project
# under your home directory (Telescope find_files + live_grep use ripgrep).
#
# Use it to RE-INCLUDE files that are gitignored but you still want to search.
# A line starting with `!` un-ignores (re-includes) a pattern; a bare pattern
# ignores it. This is the "sweetspot": .gitignore keeps node_modules/build/cache
# dirs out (fast, like VSCode), while the rules below pull the useful bits back.

# --- Environment files (usually gitignored, but we DO want to search them) ---
!.env
!.env.*
!*.env
!.envrc

# Add more re-includes here as needed, e.g.:
# !.npmrc
# !config/secrets.example.yml
